IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VIII.5 (Temporary Measures to Facilitate Access to Benefits):
-- the heading "Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations" (ss 153.1922 to 153.1925): eligibility, determined earnings,
-- the qualifying period and access to special benefits for a fisher.
-- Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Seat: a fisher who asks whether they qualify for benefits, on what earnings, and how often.
--
-- The Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations are not among the inputs. What the Act says about them (sections 8,
-- 8.1 and 12 of those Regulations) is a plain input here.
--
-- CESSATION. Sections 153.1922 to 153.1924 cease to apply on December 18, 2021 (s 153.196(3)); section 153.1925 ceases
-- with the rest of the Part (s 153.196(1)). Each rule takes the BOOLEAN "has not ceased to apply under section 153.196"
-- from `s 153.196 the provision applies on the day` with the right group.

§ `The periods of section 153.1923`

-- The four periods in which an earlier benefit period of a fisher counts. Each is a Period of days with both ends included.
-- src:3045 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 29, 2019 and ending on June 20, 2020, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) (src:3045)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2019 9 29), (YMD 2020 6 20)

-- src:3046 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 30, 2018 and ending on June 15, 2019; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(a)(iii) (src:3046)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.1923(1)(a)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2018 9 30), (YMD 2019 6 15)

-- src:3049 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 29, 2020 and ending on December 19, 2020, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(b)(ii) (src:3049)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.1923(1)(b)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2020 3 29), (YMD 2020 12 19)

-- src:3050 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 31, 2019 and ending on December 21, 2019.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(b)(iii) (src:3050)
GIVETH A `Period of days`
`s 153.1923(1)(b)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YMD 2019 3 31), (YMD 2019 12 21)

-- src:3047 | (b) in the case of an initial claim for benefits made on or after March 28, 2021 under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(b) (src:3047)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 153.1923(1)(b) the first day on which an initial claim may be made` MEANS YMD 2021 3 28

§ `Section 153.1922 - eligibility`

-- Whether a day falls in any of the four periods: "the periods referred to in subparagraph 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) or (iii)
-- or (b)(ii) or (iii)".
-- src:3040 | 153.1922 A fisher who does not meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations may receive benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations if the fisher has received such benefits during any of the periods referred to in subparagraph 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) or (b)(ii) or (iii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1922 (src:3040)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1922 the day falls within one of the periods referred to in subparagraph 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) or (b)(ii) or (iii)` IF
       `the day` day `falls within` `s 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`
    OR `the day` day `falls within` `s 153.1923(1)(a)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`
    OR `the day` day `falls within` `s 153.1923(1)(b)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`
    OR `the day` day `falls within` `s 153.1923(1)(b)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`

-- A fisher who does not meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Fishing Regulations may receive
-- benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations if they received such benefits during one of the periods. A fisher
-- who does meet the conditions is not helped by this section (the Regulations decide), so the rule is about this
-- section only.
-- src:3040 | 153.1922 A fisher who does not meet the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations may receive benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations if the fisher has received such benefits during any of the periods referred to in subparagraph 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) or (b)(ii) or (iii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1922 (src:3040)
GIVEN `section 153.1922 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `meets the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day on which the fisher received benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1922 the fisher may receive benefits under section 8.1 of the Fishing Regulations by virtue of this section` IF
        `section 153.1922 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND NOT (`meets the conditions under paragraph 8(2)(b) or (7)(b) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`)
    AND `s 153.1922 the day falls within one of the periods referred to in subparagraph 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) or (iii) or (b)(ii) or (iii)` `a day on which the fisher received benefits under section 8.1 of those Regulations`

§ `Section 153.1923 - determined earnings`

DECLARE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher` HAS
    `ei6 day on which the earlier benefit period was established`                        IS A DATE
    `ei6 earnings used to calculate the rate of weekly benefits for the earlier benefit period` IS A NUMBER

-- The earnings of an earlier benefit period count only if it was established within the period the paragraph names.
-- src:3045 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 29, 2019 and ending on June 20, 2020, and
-- src:3046 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 30, 2018 and ending on June 15, 2019; and
-- src:3049 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 29, 2020 and ending on December 19, 2020, and
-- src:3050 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 31, 2019 and ending on December 21, 2019.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1) (src:3045-3046) (src:3049-3050)
GIVEN earlier IS A MAYBE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher`
      period IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1923(1) the earnings of the earlier benefit period if it was established within the period` IS
    CONSIDER earlier
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF `the day` (e's `ei6 day on which the earlier benefit period was established`) `falls within` period
        THEN JUST (e's `ei6 earnings used to calculate the rate of weekly benefits for the earlier benefit period`)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- The highest of the earnings that exist.
-- src:3042 | 153.1923 (1) The rate of weekly benefits under section 8.1 of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations shall be calculated using the highest of the following earnings:
-- src:3047 | (b) in the case of an initial claim for benefits made on or after March 28, 2021 under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1) (src:3042) (src:3047)
GIVEN first IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      second IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      third IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1923(1) the highest of the earnings that exist` IS
    IF null (mapMaybe (GIVEN m YIELD m) (LIST first, second, third))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (maximum (mapMaybe (GIVEN m YIELD m) (LIST first, second, third)))

-- (a): an initial claim under subsection 8(1) of the Fishing Regulations: the highest of (i) the earnings that would be
-- used, if applicable, (ii) those used for the benefit period established under 8(1) in the first period, and (iii) in
-- the second.
-- src:3043 | (a) in the case of an initial claim for benefits under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations,
-- src:3044 | (i) if applicable, the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits,
-- src:3045 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 29, 2019 and ending on June 20, 2020, and
-- src:3046 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(1) of those Regulations during the period beginning on September 30, 2018 and ending on June 15, 2019; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(a) (src:3043-3046)
GIVEN `section 153.1923 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher's rate of weekly benefits, if applicable` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(1) in the period of subparagraph (ii)` IS A MAYBE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher`
      `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(1) in the period of subparagraph (iii)` IS A MAYBE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1923(1)(a) the earnings on which the rate of weekly benefits is calculated, for an initial claim under subsection 8(1)` IS
    IF `section 153.1923 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    THEN `s 153.1923(1) the highest of the earnings that exist`
            `the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher's rate of weekly benefits, if applicable`
            (`s 153.1923(1) the earnings of the earlier benefit period if it was established within the period` `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(1) in the period of subparagraph (ii)` `s 153.1923(1)(a)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`)
            (`s 153.1923(1) the earnings of the earlier benefit period if it was established within the period` `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(1) in the period of subparagraph (iii)` `s 153.1923(1)(a)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (b): an initial claim made on or after March 28, 2021 under subsection 8(6) of the Fishing Regulations, with the
-- periods of (b)(ii) and (iii).
-- src:3047 | (b) in the case of an initial claim for benefits made on or after March 28, 2021 under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations,
-- src:3048 | (i) if applicable, the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits,
-- src:3049 | (ii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 29, 2020 and ending on December 19, 2020, and
-- src:3050 | (iii) the earnings that were used to calculate the fisher’s rate of weekly benefits for the benefit period that was established for the fisher under subsection 8(6) of those Regulations during the period beginning on March 31, 2019 and ending on December 21, 2019.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(1)(b) (src:3047-3050)
GIVEN `section 153.1923 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made` IS A DATE
      `the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher's rate of weekly benefits, if applicable` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(6) in the period of subparagraph (ii)` IS A MAYBE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher`
      `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(6) in the period of subparagraph (iii)` IS A MAYBE `ei6 Earlier benefit period of a fisher`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1923(1)(b) the earnings on which the rate of weekly benefits is calculated, for an initial claim under subsection 8(6)` IS
    IF     `section 153.1923 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
       AND `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made` AT LEAST `s 153.1923(1)(b) the first day on which an initial claim may be made`
    THEN `s 153.1923(1) the highest of the earnings that exist`
            `the earnings that would be used to calculate the fisher's rate of weekly benefits, if applicable`
            (`s 153.1923(1) the earnings of the earlier benefit period if it was established within the period` `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(6) in the period of subparagraph (ii)` `s 153.1923(1)(b)(ii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`)
            (`s 153.1923(1) the earnings of the earlier benefit period if it was established within the period` `the earlier benefit period established under subsection 8(6) in the period of subparagraph (iii)` `s 153.1923(1)(b)(iii) the period in which the earlier benefit period must have been established`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): a fisher may have a benefit period established once under paragraph (1)(a) and once under paragraph (1)(b).
-- src:3052 | (2) A fisher may have a benefit period established once under paragraph (1)(a) and once under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(2) (src:3052)
GIVEN `the number of benefit periods already established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1923(2) a benefit period may be established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(a)` IF
    `the number of benefit periods already established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(a)` LESS THAN 1

-- src:3052 | (2) A fisher may have a benefit period established once under paragraph (1)(a) and once under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1923(2) (src:3052)
GIVEN `the number of benefit periods already established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1923(2) a benefit period may be established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(b)` IF
    `the number of benefit periods already established for the fisher under paragraph (1)(b)` LESS THAN 1

§ `Sections 153.1924 and 153.1925 - qualifying period and special benefits`

-- 153.1924: for the Fishing Regulations the earnings determined under 153.1923(1) are the insurable earnings for the
-- qualifying period.
-- src:3054 | 153.1924 For the purposes of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, the earnings determined under subsection 153.1923(1) are the insurable earnings for the qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1924 (src:3054)
GIVEN `section 153.1924 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings determined under subsection 153.1923(1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 153.1924 the insurable earnings for the qualifying period` IS
    IF `section 153.1924 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    THEN `the earnings determined under subsection 153.1923(1)`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 153.1925: despite subsection 12(1) of the Fishing Regulations, an insured person who is not qualified under section 7
-- and who is claiming special benefits qualifies for them if they have at least $2,500 of insurable earnings from
-- employment as a fisher in their qualifying period. A person who does not meet this test is not thereby unqualified:
-- the Regulations may still qualify them, so FALSE here means only "not by this section".
-- src:3056 | 153.1925 Despite subsection 12(1) of the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations, an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7 and who is claiming special benefits qualifies to receive the special benefits if the person has at least $2,500 of insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 153.1925 (src:3056)
GIVEN `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is claiming special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 153.1925 the insured person qualifies to receive the special benefits by this section` IF
        `Part VIII.5 has not ceased to apply under section 153.196`
    AND `is an insured person who is not qualified to receive benefits under section 7`
    AND `is claiming special benefits`
    AND `the insurable earnings from employment as a fisher in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 2500
